WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.410
Marketing mix modelling feeds in years of weekly sales,

00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:04.260
spend,

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:05.050
price,

00:00:04.969 --> 00:00:05.839
seasonality,

00:00:05.889 --> 00:00:07.584
the economy and competitors.

00:00:07.634 --> 00:00:09.247
Out comes what drove sales,

00:00:09.297 --> 00:00:10.533
the return by channel,

00:00:10.583 --> 00:00:12.160
and where the next dollar goes.

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:14.914
It's Bayesian, and privacy safe.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.239
Think of predicting who'll watch the next episode.

00:00:18.289 --> 00:00:20.432
You start with what you know about viewers,

00:00:20.482 --> 00:00:23.030
then update as evidence comes in.

00:00:23.733 --> 00:00:25.700
No individual is tracked.

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:27.044
It reads the whole market,

00:00:27.094 --> 00:00:28.636
so it looks less precise,

00:00:28.686 --> 00:00:30.395
but it's more honest.

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:32.276
Use it like this:

00:00:32.326 --> 00:00:33.126
explain the inputs and outputs,

00:00:32.763 --> 00:00:37.274
then move the next dollar where it works hardest.
